  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 135 PM EST Tue Nov 24 2026\n\nPattern Synopsis and Forecast:\n\nHeights aloft will continue to fill in through the rest of the day \nand into tonight. At the same time, two pieces of energy flow across \nthe central and southern portions of the country. First is an upper \nlow that dives across the Mid MS Valley and eventually OH Valley on \nThursday, and another is across the Southeast Gulf Coast. These \nfeatures interact to a degree, with sfc low pressure developing \nacross Appalachia (becoming an inland cutter). The location and \ntrajectory of these upper and sfc features will result in an \nintrusion of southwest to northeast moisture/lift and thus \nprecipitation chances. Ensemble guidance continues to show a gradient \nin the precipitation across northern MI, EPS/GEPS showing modest \nprecip across Saginaw Bay and northeast lower with very little \nacross portions of northwest lower and the eastern UP. Our current \nforecast follows this thought process with generally minor to modest \nrainfall accumulations. Precipitation chances generally hold off \nuntil later Thursday and especially Thursday night and remain into \nFriday. Thursday night into Friday, the higher terrain could very \nwell mix wet snow, but any snow accums look either minimal or non-\nexistent based on the thermal profiles, ensemble 50th percentile \nsnow accums, and the fact that the heavier precipitation rates will \nlikely remain to the east. \n\nA few showers may linger on Saturday as weak energy moves through \nthe westerly flow. We watch another piece of energy diving out of \nthe southern Plains for the second half of the weekend which could \nproduce predominantly rain showers, perhaps another mix/wet snow \novernight across the higher terrain. Impact seems pretty low overall \nthough as any injection of true cold air seems to be locked up way \nto the north of N MI.\n\nTemperatures will be seasonable through Wednesday (mid 30s to low \n40s for highs), with low to mid 40s late week and into the weekend.",
